# Example: field paths in a method

Walk into another object with dots. PlayArea is Rect, so the ball's walls are playArea.rect.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Ball 100 100 1 1 5]
]
```

## Methods

```
Game::inBounds = {
  (ball.x > playArea.rect.x) and (ball.x < (playArea.rect.x + playArea.rect.width))
}
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = gameFactory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("inBounds");
    trace(assemblage.inBounds());
}
```
